    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Advantages of rapid onsite evaluation (ROSE) for molecular testing of pancreaticobiliary cytological specimens</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "María D. Lozano",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 347.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"463\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Specimen adequacy</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Preliminary diagnosis</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Triage for ancillary studies</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Careful control of preanalytics</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Real-time guidance to the physician performing the FNAB procedure</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Ability to stop sampling when appropriate material has been obtained</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Clinicopathological communication</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 17.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Possibility of sampling/testing different sites</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Note: ROSE is not needed in cystic lesions.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
